{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":31068,"ns":0,"title":"Analogy of the divided line","extract":"The analogy of the divided line (Ancient Greek: γραμμὴ δίχα τετμημένη, romanized: grammē dicha tetmēmenē) is presented by the Greek philosopher Plato in the Republic (509d–511e). It is written as a dialogue between Glaucon and Socrates, in which the latter further elaborates upon the immediately preceding analogy of the Sun at the former's request.","description":"Platonic philosophical analogy","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}